      "ok": true,
      "answer": "Here's what you can afford with Eval Hero's **25 gold** at Prosperity 1 (items 001–016 available):\n\n---\n\n## ✅ Affordable (25g or less)\n\n| # | Name | Slot | Cost | Effect |\n|---|------|------|------|--------|\n| 001 | Weathered Boots | Legs | 15g | During your move ability, add *Move +1*. |\n| 002 | Winged Shoes | Legs | 15g | During your turn, add *Jump* to all your move abilities. |\n| 003 | Hide Armor | Body | 10g | On the next two sources of damage from attacks targeting you, gain *Shield 1* for the attacks. |\n| 004 | Leather Armor | Body | 10g | When you are attacked, before drawing an attack modifier card, the attacker gains *Disadvantage*. |\n| 005 | Scouting Lens | Head | 10g | During your attack ability, add *Pierce 1* to one attack. |\n| 006 | Amulet of Life | Head | 15g | During your turn, perform *Heal 1, Self*. |\n| 007 | Poison Dagger | One Hand | 15g | During your melee attack ability, add *Poison* to one attack. |\n| 008 | Heater Shield | One Hand | 15g | When you suffer damage from an attack, gain *Shield 1* for the attack. |\n| 009 | Focusing Rod | One Hand | 10g | During your turn, if you've performed an action with Lost, perform *Heal 1, Range 3*. |\n| 010 | Simple Bow | Two Hands | 15g | During your ranged attack ability, gain *Advantage* on one attack. |\n| 011 | Healing Potion | Small Item | 10g | During your turn, perform *Heal 3, Self*. |\n| 012 | Stamina Potion | Small Item | 10g | During your turn, recover one level 1 card from your discard pile. |\n| 013 | Element Potion | Small Item | 10g | During your turn, *Wild* (element). |\n\n---\n\n## ❌ Too Expensive\n\n| # | Name | Slot | Cost |\n|---|------|------|------|\n| 014 | Studded Leather | Body | 20g |\n| 015 | Comfortable Shoes | Legs | 20g |\n| 016 | Circlet of Elements | Head | 20g |\n\n---\n\n**Note:** Items 014–016 cost 20g, which is under 25g — so actually **you can afford those too!** All 16 items in the Prosperity 1 shop are within your 25g budget. However, you can only buy **one item** before running out of gold for a second purchase in most cases. Items 003–013 (10g each) would let you buy **two** if both cost 10g (total 20g).\n\n*(Source: GHS Card Data, Gloomhaven 2nd Edition)*",
